FACT 2 DETECTION:
  For AP: P_k ≈ (n-2)/n at each step (no improvement, Fact 2 silent).
  For non-AP: SOME intermediate P_k > (n-2)/n (Fact 2 active!).

  Fact 2 says: clearing runner k EXCLUDES configurations where
  other runners create cycles that would pull k back into danger.
  This exclusion INCREASES the conditional clearance for runner k+1.

  For AP: the runners are perfectly distributed, so Fact 2 has no
  additional effect (no cycles to exclude — already transitive-like).
  For non-AP: the runners have arithmetic asymmetries that create
  potential cycles. Fact 2 EXCLUDES these cycles, improving clearance.

