CYCLE EXCLUSION INSIGHT:
  When a runner is cleared (enters safe zone), all 3-cycles
  passing through it are BROKEN. Fact 2 says these broken cycles
  can't re-form — the cleared runner's outgoing arc (observer→runner)
  prevents the reverse direction.

  The number of excluded cycles per clearance = the 'Fact 2 bonus'
  for the conditional probability of the next step.

  For AP: cycles are minimal (near-transitive) → small bonus.
  For non-AP: cycles are more numerous → larger bonus.

